## Build 5 adds full extrinsic (coherent-score) marginalization to the microlensed likelihood so the ~15-D lensed posterior collapses to a ~9-10-D intrinsic+lens sampled space and samples in hours, not the measured ~1 day. Professor ruling (cited): ship FULL extrinsic marginalization with CoherentScoreHM directly — a distance(+22-only-phase)-only tier does NOT move wall-clock because the dominant per-proposal cost is XPHM coarse-strain generation, incurred once per lnlike regardless of how many extrinsic dims are marginalized analytically; only full extrinsic marginalization does the sky/time/psi/distance/phase integral by QMC from ONE matched-filter timeseries per intrinsic+lens proposal. HM (not QAS) is mandatory because it respects the Build-2 22-only phase constraint structurally. Core physics (Professor-confirmed): the lensed matched-filter timeseries is a sum over images of TIME-SHIFTED, kernel-weighted copies of the unlensed per-mode timeseries — since F(w)=Σ_a e^{i w τ_a} K_a(w) with w=c_lens·f linear in f, e^{i w τ_a}=e^{i 2π dt_a f} is an EXACT timeseries shift by dt_a=c_lens·τ_a/2π. So we override the existing `_get_dh_hh_timeshift` seam: modulate the unlensed bin templates by k0_a[b]·e^{i2π dt_a f_b} per image and contract against the UNCHANGED `_d_h_weights` (data side, exact), and scale `_h_h_weights` by |F(w_b)|^2 (norm side, valid under the lens-aware bin guard). Simplifier verdicts: A2 composition (the marginalized class holds an internal LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood purely to call `_amplification_coefficients`; the one-time unused CBC-moment build is cheaper and far safer than a mixin-refactor of the validated 1500-line likelihood.py); reuse `LensedPosterior` unchanged (it already maps LensDomainError/CancellationError→-inf); new module `cogwheel/lensing/marginalized_likelihood.py`; 2 new classes total (likelihood + registered prior); no QAS variant. Documented deferrals (approved, matching the prior d_app-deferral precedent): the coherent score marginalizes the overall amplitude and yields APPARENT distance d_app=d_luminosity/√μ_macro; the physical transform d_L=d_app·√μ_macro (μ_macro=1/((1-κ)²-γ²), F009) and any apparent-vs-physical distance-prior reweighting are documented and deferred to post-analysis, NOT relabeled in the pipeline. Refusals are evaluated ONCE up front per proposal and propagate to -inf at the posterior boundary — never averaged inside the QMC integral. The engine (chang_refsdal/), the plain LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood path and its gates, and the coherent-score numba internals/lookup-table formats are all consumed UNCHANGED. Post-build (driver): a real marginalized sampling run is the wall-clock headline (target hours), followed by the deferred injection-recovery/PP validation.

### WP1: LensedMarginalizedExtrinsicLikelihood (coherent-score marginalization)
  What: Create the new module cogwheel/lensing/marginalized_likelihood.py defining LensedMarginalizedExtrinsicLikelihood(BaseMarginalizedExtrinsicLikelihood). It composes an internal LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood to obtain the per-image amplification (delays, per-bin kernel coefficients) and produces the lensed per-mode/per-pol matched-filter timeseries (dh_mptd) and norm (hh_mppd) that CoherentScoreHM consumes, reusing the unlensed-fiducial summary weights unchanged. Consume the coherent score and lookup tables UNMODIFIED. Export the class in cogwheel/lensing/__init__.py. Do NOT author any tests (Test Developer owns all new tests).
  Where: NEW cogwheel/lensing/marginalized_likelihood.py; edit cogwheel/lensing/__init__.py. Read for reference (do not edit): cogwheel/likelihood/marginalized_extrinsic.py (BaseMarginalizedExtrinsicLikelihood: __init__, _set_summary, _set_d_h_weights, _set_h_h_weights, _get_dh_hh_timeshift, _create_coherent_score, lnlike_and_metadata, get_blob, postprocess_samples), cogwheel/lensing/likelihood.py (LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood: _amplification_coefficients, _image_delays, _lens_params, _check_candidate_delays, delta_t_max, _validate_bin_delay_criterion, __getstate__), cogwheel/likelihood/marginalization/coherent_score_hm.py (CoherentScoreHM inputs).
  How: SUBCLASS BaseMarginalizedExtrinsicLikelihood (it extends BaseLinearFree, giving `_get_linearfree_hplus_hcross_dt`, `_set_summary` that builds `_d_h_weights` (m,t,d,b) and `_h_h_weights` (m,d,b) against the UNLENSED fiducial `par_dic_0`, `_ref_dic`, `asd_drift`, `_create_coherent_score`, `lnlike_and_metadata`, `get_blob`, `postprocess_samples`). (1) __init__: signature `(event_data, waveform_generator, par_dic_0, delta_t_max, *, fbin=None, pn_phase_tol=None, spline_degree=3, t_range=(-.07,.07), coherent_score=None, dlnl_marginalized_threshold=30., bin_delay_tol=<engine default>, kernel_subsamples=<engine default>)`. Call super().__init__(...) FIRST (this sets self.fbin, the unlensed summaries, coherent score, asd_drift). THEN build the internal engine on the SAME bins: `self._engine = LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood(event_data, waveform_generator, par_dic_0, delta_t_max, fbin=self.fbin, spline_degree=spline_degree, bin_delay_tol=bin_delay_tol, kernel_subsamples=kernel_subsamples)`; store delta_t_max/bin_delay_tol/kernel_subsamples. Do NOT accept the engine as an __init__ argument — JSONMixin round-trips via get_init_dict from primitives, so the engine must be rebuilt inside __init__. Constructing the engine on self.fbin re-runs the lens-aware bin guard (`_validate_bin_delay_criterion` → LensedBinningError if π·Δf_bin·delta_t_max breaches tol); let that propagate at construction — it is the desired guard. Document the outer/inner constructor-signature coupling in a comment (Simplifier watch flag). (2) `_create_coherent_score`: mirror MarginalizedExtrinsicLikelihood._create_coherent_score EXACTLY — build a CoherentScoreHM from a SkyDictionary over event_data.detector_names, m_arr from waveform_generator, distance-only LookupTable; the coherent score is consumed UNCHANGED (never touch marginalization/). (3) `params` property: read MarginalizedExtrinsicLikelihood.params to get the exact set of extrinsic keys it removes from waveform_generator.params; return `sorted(set(self._engine.params) - _MARGINALIZED_EXTRINSIC)` where _MARGINALIZED_EXTRINSIC is that same removed set — this keeps intrinsic CBC + the 7 standard lens params (m_lens_msun, z_lens, y1, y2, gamma, beta, kappa) and drops distance/phase/sky/time/psi (iota stays sampled, as in the unlensed HM intrinsic prior). (4) OVERRIDE `_get_dh_hh_timeshift(self, par_dic)`: (a) evaluate the lens engine ONCE up front — `lens = self._engine._lens_params(par_dic)`; `delays, k0, k1, partition = self._engine._amplification_coefficients(par_dic)`; `self._engine._check_candidate_delays(delays)`; `dt = self._engine._image_delays(lens, partition)` (per-image detector-frame delays [s]). Do NOT catch LensDomainError/CancellationError — they must propagate to the posterior boundary. (b) build unlensed bin templates exactly as the base: `h_mpb, timeshift = self._get_linearfree_hplus_hcross_dt(dict(par_dic)|self._ref_dic, by_m=True)` (n_m,2,n_b). (c) with `f_b = self.fbin`, per image a form `mod_a[b] = k0[...,a][b] * exp(1j*2*pi*dt[a]*f_b)` (confirm k0 axis order from _amplification_coefficients — it is per-bin per-channel), and modulated template `h_a = h_mpb * mod_a[None,None,:]`. (d) DATA: `dh_mptd = Σ_a (self._d_h_weights[:,None] @ h_a.conj()[:,:,None,:,None])[...,0]` — accumulate the sum over images; this is the exact image-summed, dt_a-shifted, K_a-weighted lensed timeseries because the linear phase at bin frequencies maps through the existing weights to a pure timeseries shift. (e) NORM: `F_b = Σ_a k0[...,a][b] * exp(1j*2*pi*dt[a]*f_b)` (n_b, complex); `modF2 = abs(F_b)**2` (real); `w_hh = self._h_h_weights * modF2[None,None,:]`; then reuse the base einsum `hh_mppd = einsum('mdb,mpb,mPb->mpPd', w_hh, h_mpb[m_inds], h_mpb.conj()[mprime_inds])` with `m_inds, mprime_inds = self.waveform_generator.get_m_mprime_inds()`. Use the UNLENSED h_mpb for the modes; |F|^2 carries all lensing because F is a mode-independent scalar — this is exact under the bin guard. (f) apply `psd_drift_correction = self.asd_drift**-2`, cast to complex64/float32 as the base does, return `dh_mptd, hh_mppd, timeshift`. Add a concise physics comment stating F(w)=Σ_a e^{i w τ_a}K_a(w), w=c_lens·f ⇒ e^{i w τ_a}=e^{i2π dt_a f} exact shift; data=Σ_a shifted-weighted timeseries; norm=|F|²-weighted single-bin, valid under π·Δf_bin·delta_t_max<bin_delay_tol. (5) Distance labeling: KEEP inherited get_blob/postprocess_samples (do not relabel the coherent score's 'd_luminosity' column — relabeling breaks lnl_aux/plotting); add a loud docstring note that the marginalized/drawn distance is APPARENT distance d_app=d_luminosity/√μ_macro and that physical d_L=d_app·√μ_macro (μ_macro=1/((1-κ)²-γ²), F009) plus apparent-vs-physical distance-prior reweighting are DEFERRED to post-analysis. (6) Pickling: rely on the internal engine's existing __getstate__ (it drops its transient _fid_cache); default pickle recursion of self._engine is therefore safe — add explicit __getstate__/__setstate__ only if a smoke pickle round-trip shows the cache is not dropped.
