### Professor Inputs
  - TIERING: ship FULL extrinsic marginalization (CoherentScoreHM) directly; do NOT ship a distance(+phase)-only tier. Distance/phase marginalization removes only 1-2 sampled dims but the dominant per-proposal cost (XPHM coarse-strain generation + lens engine) is unchanged, giving ~1.3x (1 day -> ~18 h, misses target). Full extrinsic marginalization drops ~6 extrinsic dims AND does the sky/time/psi/distance/phase integral by QMC from ONE matched-filter timeseries per intrinsic+lens proposal -> ~9-D sampled, estimated ~2-5 h (meets the hours target).
  - LENSED TIMESERIES: z_m^lensed(t) = sum_a <d | K_a(w) h_m>(t - dt_a) is CORRECT. Because w = c_lens*f is linear in f, exp(i w tau_a) = exp(i 2π dt_a f) is an EXACT frequency-domain linear phase = timeseries shift by dt_a = c_lens*tau_a/(2π). K_a(w) is NOT a pure phase (carries magnitude+Morse phase+diffraction), so it must be folded into the template before the matched filter — build n_img time-shifted, K_a-weighted per-image contractions and SUM. Heterodyne against the UNLENSED fiducial h0 (baking a lensed fiducial would force per-proposal summary rebuilds).
  - NORM: hh_mppd is the same image double-sum the plain lensed likelihood already contracts; because F is a mode-independent scalar it reduces to multiplying the per-bin norm weights by |F(w_b)|^2 (single-bin, valid under the lens-aware bin guard pi*Delta_f_bin*delta_t_max < bin_delay_tol). hh has no time axis (correct — (h|h) has no time-shift freedom). Reuse the existing norm construction; only the data-side timeseries needs the per-image time-shift treatment.
  - REFUSAL SEMANTICS: evaluate the lens engine (F, delays, kernels) ONCE up front per proposal; a LensDomainError/CancellationError must map to lnL=-inf at the posterior boundary and the coherent score must NEVER be invoked for a refusing config — no refusal may be silently averaged inside the QMC. Partial-image failure => full refusal (F is a single physical function). Let exceptions propagate to LensedPosterior (Build-4 pattern), do not catch-and-continue.
  - ACCURACY ORACLE + TOLERANCES: full-marg gate |median(lnL_marg over ~20 evals) - lnL_oracle| <= 0.3 nats with 90th-percentile eval spread <= 0.2 nats (QMC error ~3.4*n_eff^-0.76, ~0.14 nats at n_eff=100). Oracle = importance sampling of the plain lnlike over the 6-D extrinsic block (~2-3e4 draws, n_eff>~500 => oracle <~0.1 nats), NOT a full 10^8 grid. Use 3 representative configs (two-image, near-cusp, deep-macro) for a minutes-scale in-build gate; full 8-config sweep is optional/nightly.
  - 22-ONLY PHASE CONSTRAINT: must use CoherentScoreHM (higher-mode path: distance-only LookupTable + orbital-phase quadrature over nphi), NOT the QAS m=2 variant — this respects the constant-lens-phase ~ orbital-phase degeneracy being 22-only for XPHM higher modes.
  - d_app: the coherent score marginalizes overall amplitude and yields APPARENT distance d_app = d_L/sqrt(mu_macro) (F009: F(w->0)->sqrt(mu_macro) folds into apparent distance); the distance LookupTable machinery applies with d_app in place of d_L; physical d_L = d_app*sqrt(mu_macro) is a documented post-analysis transform.
  - CONDITIONAL DRAWS: cheapest test that catches a wrong conditional is round-trip likelihood consistency — draw N=50 extrinsic per config, evaluate full plain lnlike; require max(lnL_full) >= lnL_marg - 0.3, mean >= lnL_marg - 0.5, none > lnL_marg + 0.5; supplement with a single-config KS check of d_app and t_geocenter marginals vs a 1D/2D grid slice.

### Domain Test Descriptions
  - UNLENSED-LIMIT TIMESERIES IDENTITY (F009-aware). Setup: build LensedMarginalizedExtrinsicLikelihood and the stock unlensed MarginalizedExtrinsicLikelihood on the SAME seeded EventData + IMRPhenomXPHM WaveformGenerator + par_dic_0 + fbin; choose lens params in the strictly unsheared limit gamma=kappa=0 with m_lens small so w->0 and F identically 1 (per F009, only gamma=kappa=0 gives F==1 — do NOT use sheared configs here). Operation: for a seeded intrinsic par_dic, compute (dh_mptd, hh_mppd) from both classes. Expected: lensed dh_mptd and hh_mppd equal the unlensed ones to rtol ~1e-6 (single image, K=1, dt=0). Diagnostic: heatmap of |Δdh_mptd| over (t,detector) reveals a spurious per-image shift (horizontal band) or kernel-amplitude error.
  - SINGLE-IMAGE TIME-SHIFT CORRECTNESS (F002-independent oracle). Setup: a two-image lens config with a known non-zero relative delay; obtain the independent per-image (dt_a, K_a) decomposition ONLY from LensedWaveformGenerator.decompose / geometry+operator (NEVER from the marginalized class under test). Operation: build the marginalized dh_mptd and compare against a manual reference = sum over images of the unlensed per-mode timeseries scaled by K_a(w_b) and shifted by dt_a (implemented by folding exp(i2π dt_a f_b) into the template and contracting with the stock _d_h_weights, or by explicit time-domain roll). Expected: agreement to rtol ~1e-6. Diagnostic: overlay Re/Im z_m(t) for the two constructions — a delay error appears as a horizontal offset, a kernel error as an amplitude/phase mismatch. Include an AST/import guard forbidding the module-under-test's names in the oracle.
  - MARGINALIZED lnL vs IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING BRUTE-FORCE ORACLE (Professor tolerances). Setup: 3 representative seeded configs — (C_two) two-image moderate fringe, 30+30 Msun, SNR~20; (C_cusp) near-cusp 4-image, 60+60 Msun; (C_macro) deep-macro gamma~0.3, w_min~1. Oracle: integrate the PLAIN LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood.lnlike over the 6-D extrinsic block (d_luminosity, phi_ref, t_geocenter, ra, dec, psi) by importance sampling — draw ~2-3e4 extrinsic points from a broad proposal centered on truth (~3x posterior width), reweight by exp(lnlike - ln_proposal), lnL_oracle = logsumexp(...) - log(N); report n_eff and require n_eff >~ 500 so oracle precision <~0.1 nats. Operation: evaluate LensedMarginalizedExtrinsicLikelihood.lnlike 20x with distinct fixed seeds per config; take the median. Expected: |median(lnL_marg) - lnL_oracle| <= 0.3 nats per config, and the spread of the 20 evals has 90th-percentile deviation from the median <= 0.2 nats. Diagnostic: scatter of the 20 marg evals against the oracle band — bias shows as a constant offset, under-converged QMC as wide scatter. Keep this test to the 3 configs for a minutes-scale gate; a full 8-config sweep (C1-C8) is an optional slow/nightly variant.
  - PLAIN-vs-MARGINALIZED CONSISTENCY BY REWEIGHTING. Setup: one seeded config; draw ~200 full (intrinsic+lens+extrinsic) points from the plain LensedIASPrior at the fixed intrinsic+lens point (extrinsic varying). Operation: compute plain LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood.lnlike for each, and separately the marginalized lnL at the shared intrinsic+lens point; verify that log of the extrinsic-prior-weighted mean of exp(plain lnlike) matches lnL_marg. Expected: agreement within 0.3 nats (report Monte-Carlo error). Diagnostic: running-mean convergence plot of the reweighted evidence approaching lnL_marg.
  - REFUSAL CONTRACT — REFUSE BEFORE THE INTEGRAL. Setup: (i) a macro-saddle config (1-kappa <= |gamma|) that raises geometry.LensDomainError, and (ii) a cancellation-band config that raises operator.CancellationError. Operation: instrument the likelihood's coherent_score with a spy/patch counting get_marginalization_info calls, then evaluate via LensedMarginalizedExtrinsicLikelihood / LensedPosterior. Expected: the posterior returns lnL = -inf (exact, no NaN) and the coherent-score get_marginalization_info call-count is 0 for the refusing config — the engine refusal propagates BEFORE extrinsic marginalization. Mutation check: wrapping the engine call in a swallowing try/except (returning finite) must turn this test RED. Diagnostic: assertion-only; confirm exact -inf and zero coherent-score calls.
  - CONDITIONAL-DRAW ROUND-TRIP CONSISTENCY (Professor spec). Setup: 3 seeded intrinsic+lens configs; run the marginalized likelihood to get marg_info; draw N=50 seeded conditional extrinsic samples via gen_samples_from_marg_info. Operation: for each drawn extrinsic sample evaluate the FULL plain LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood.lnlike at (intrinsic+lens+drawn extrinsic). Expected: max(lnL_full) >= lnL_marg - 0.3; mean(lnL_full) >= lnL_marg - 0.5; no draw exceeds lnL_marg + 0.5. Diagnostic: histogram of lnL_full with lnL_marg marked — a biased conditional (wrong sky/distance/time) puts the mass far below lnL_marg. Supplementary (1 config, ~500 draws): KS-test the drawn d_luminosity(=d_app) and t_geocenter marginals against a direct 1D/2D grid slice at fixed intrinsic (p > 0.01).
  - NORM-PATH CROSS-CHECK AGAINST THE PLAIN LIKELIHOOD. Setup: a seeded lensed config. Operation: compare the marginalized |F(w_b)|^2-weighted norm construction against the plain LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood._get_dh_hh_no_asd_drift (h_L|h_L) at a matched extrinsic point (collapse hh_mppd with the reference antenna factors, or compare the per-bin |F(w_b)|^2 integrand to the plain decomposition's reconstructed |F|^2). Expected: reproduction of the plain (h_L|h_L) to the bin-approximation tolerance rtol ~1e-3 (matching the fast-path interpolation gate). Diagnostic: overlay per-bin |F(w_b)|^2 (marginalized) on the plain-decomposition |F|^2 — divergence flags a delay-difference / bin-guard problem.
  - DETERMINISM, REGISTRATION, PRIOR PAIRING, SERIALIZATION. Setup: instantiate LensedMarginalizedExtrinsicIASPrior and the paired likelihood. Expected: (a) the prior is present in gw_prior.prior_registry; (b) prior.standard_params == likelihood.params exactly (set equality); (c) 1e3 seeded prior draws all lie inside the certified lens domain and yield finite-or-exact-(-inf) posterior values with zero NaN; (d) the marginalized lnL is bit-repeatable across two calls at the same RNG seed; (e) JSONMixin to_json/from_json round-trip of the likelihood reproduces lnL bit-for-bit (engine rebuilt from primitives, not stored as an init arg). Diagnostic: assertion-only.
  - LENS-AWARE BIN GUARD UNDER MARGINALIZATION. Setup: attempt to construct LensedMarginalizedExtrinsicLikelihood with delta_t_max large enough that pi*Delta_f_bin*delta_t_max breaches bin_delay_tol on the coarse fbin. Expected: construction raises LensedBinningError (inherited via the internal engine's _validate_bin_delay_criterion on self.fbin). Diagnostic: assertion-only; confirms the guard is active on the marginalized path, not just the plain path.

